{"name":"Venus Fest Day 02 at Allan Gardens","aliases":["Venus Fest 2026 Day 2"],"city":"toronto","date":"2026-09-19","start_date":"2026-09-19","end_date":"2026-09-20","description":"Venus Fest's second night brings queer artists, live music and dancing into Allan Gardens Conservatory with ASL interpretation and community programming.","link":"https://ra.co/events/2493921","ticket_url":"https://ra.co/events/2493921","location":"Allan Gardens Conservatory, 160 Gerrard Street East, Toronto, Ontario, Canada","lat":43.6618,"lng":-79.3747,"vibe":"lush conservatory music night centring queer artistry, access and collective joy","intel":{"entry_wait":"Advance booking is recommended for the unusual limited-capacity setting; carry valid 19+ identification and check final access notes.","best_arrival":"Reach Allan Gardens near the 21:00 opening to navigate entry and experience the full programme before the 02:00 finish.","crowd_mix":"Queer artists and audiences, independent-music fans, disabled community members, students and Toronto night-culture visitors gather.","dress_code":"There is no stated requirement; expressive evening clothing and layers suitable for a conservatory environment work well.","host_inclusivity":"The programme centres queer artists and publishes ASL interpretation, making access and representation visible parts of the night.","source_urls":["https://ra.co/events/2493921"],"research_status":"organiser_date_hours_venue_age_queer_lineup_and_asl_verified","updated_at":"2026-08-29T00:00:00Z"}},
{"name":"Massimadi Festival 2026","aliases":["Massimadi Montreal 2026","Massimadi Afro LGBTQ+ Film and Arts Festival 2026"],"city":"montreal","date":"2026-10-15","start_date":"2026-10-15","end_date":"2026-11-08","description":"Massimadi celebrates Afro LGBTQ+ cinema and arts through screenings, talks and encounters connecting Black queer stories across Montreal and the wider world.","link":"https://www.massimadi.ca/festival","ticket_url":"https://www.massimadi.ca/festival","location":"Multiple cultural venues, Montreal, Quebec, Canada","lat":45.5019,"lng":-73.5674,"vibe":"Black queer cultural festival joining film, memory, dialogue and diaspora connection","intel":{"entry_wait":"Screenings and discussions use separate capacities; consult the programme and reserve featured films or guest sessions once sales open.","best_arrival":"Follow the venue listed for each programme item and arrive before seating, especially for opening and closing events.","crowd_mix":"Black LGBTQ+ Montrealers, diasporic communities, filmmakers, artists, activists, students and francophone cinephiles attend.","dress_code":"No festival-wide code applies; comfortable cinema wear works throughout and polished personal style suits gala moments.","host_inclusivity":"Massimadi explicitly centres Afro LGBTQ+ stories, artists and audiences through cinema, arts and public conversation.","source_urls":["https://www.massimadi.ca/festival"],"research_status":"official_dates_afro_lgbtq_focus_and_city_verified","updated_at":"2026-08-29T00:00:00Z"}},
{"name":"RED Montreal – September 2026","aliases":["RED at Le Red Room September 2026"],"city":"montreal","date":"2026-09-26","start_date":"2026-09-26","end_date":"2026-09-27","description":"RED gathers Montreal's queer leather community at Le Red Room from 22:00–03:00 for progressive house under explicit respect and anti-discrimination rules.","link":"https://ra.co/events/2495697","ticket_url":"https://ra.co/events/2495697","location":"Le Red Room, 2037 Rue Saint-Denis, Montreal, Quebec, Canada","lat":45.5165,"lng":-73.5652,"vibe":"intimate leather-coded queer house night with a clear safer-floor social contract","intel":{"entry_wait":"Advance tickets are sensible for the compact room; carry valid 18+ identification and review the organiser's conduct expectations.","best_arrival":"Arrive near 22:00 for relaxed entry and the opening progression before the central after-midnight crowd.","crowd_mix":"Queer leather and fetish communities, gay men, progressive-house dancers and respectful open-minded guests share the room.","dress_code":"Leather or black clothing is suggested rather than compulsory; choose an intentional look that remains comfortable for dancing.","host_inclusivity":"The organiser calls RED a queer safe space and rejects homophobia, racism, body shaming and discriminatory conduct.","source_urls":["https://ra.co/events/2495697"],"research_status":"organiser_date_hours_venue_music_dress_and_policy_verified","updated_at":"2026-08-29T00:00:00Z"}},
